title ALES154 — Lotus's stereo_smooth_trim: the smoothed silence trim carried into stereo, two independent silences smoothed then fused into one joint cut, an edit-corner lockstep lift bound to ALES148 by the min-zero law
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Next rung after ALES153 stereo_smooth_runs (its recommend named this exactly). The ascending Lotus crux is ALES102 (smooth_trim — smooth the runs then strip the SMOOTHED silence, the speech-aware dead-air remover) carried into stereo. Crux-first and Lindy-first agree: it is the tool a keeper actually reaches for, and it fuses the two moves already proven in stereo — ALES153's per-channel smoothing and ALES148's silence intersection.
think This is an EDIT-corner lift (it changes length), so it takes ALES148's lockstep shape, NOT ALES153's per-channel analysis shape. The one line inserted into ALES148: after segmenting both channels, smooth EACH channel's runs through ALES153's smooth_runs_stereo with the shared min_run, then run the silence intersection over the SMOOTHED labels. ALES101's coverage law guarantees each smoothed run list tiles its channel's span exactly, so every jointly-silent frame is a valid original span cut exactly as ALES148 cuts. StereoSmoothTrimError = StereoSegmentError || StereoSmoothError || EditError, every fault reused by name.
think Two seams give the fusion its honesty and both are witnessed: the min-zero law (min=0 is identity smoothing, so stereo_smooth_trim collapses to ALES148's stereo_trim_silence byte for byte on both channels — proven against ALES148 directly across the frame/floor/split grid) and the lockstep law (running the mono ALES102 smooth_trim per channel desyncs to 8 and 12 where the stereo fusion holds both at 12). The crux (stereo smooth-trim law) is proven against a by-hand second implementation across five frame lengths, four floors, three splits, and six min_run values. Declick (short voiced tick jointly buried in silence removed on both, strictly shorter than min-zero) and keep-gap (short silent gap jointly between speech kept on both, strictly longer) prove the smoothing actually pays off in stereo. Degenerate and atomicity laws all GREEN.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, edits only by removing whole jointly-smoothed-silent frames through ALES2's cut in lockstep, the smoothing read-only over the labels; a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, no red. Recorded lesson: a mono FUSION rung (ALES102 = ALES96 trim + ALES101 smooth) carries into stereo by fusing the two already-lifted stereo rungs at their own corners — the smoothing runs per channel (ALES153's analysis corner, read-only over labels) and the trim intersects and cuts in lockstep (ALES148's edit corner), the seam being that the intersection reads the SMOOTHED labels instead of the raw ones. The two-family distinction (label rewrites per channel, length edits lockstep) composes cleanly: a fusion inherits each half's corner. Witness GREEN (stereo smooth-trim law across 5×4×3×6, min-zero=ALES148, declick, keep-gap, lockstep 8/12→12, degenerate, atomicity), TAME style bans clean. Front door lotus/README.md synced (ALES154 roster token appended to the Status line).
loom witness=ales_stereo_smooth_trim_witness result=GREEN laws=stereo-smooth-trim-law+min-zero-law channels=2 class=stereo-edit lift=fusion(ALES153-smooth+ALES148-intersect) form=smooth-per-channel-then-joint-lockstep-cut cases=stereo-smooth-trim-law(by-hand,5flen×4floor×3split×6min_run,balanced)+min-zero(=ALES148-byte-for-byte)+declick(joint-tick-removed-strictly-shorter)+keep-gap(joint-gap-kept-strictly-longer)+lockstep(mono-8/12→stereo-12)+degenerate(all-joint-silent-empty,no-joint-silent-unchanged)+atomicity(BadFrame/BadFrame/BadThreshold/BadFloor-untouched-balanced) reds=0
